          "realLife": "Your class attendance list is a set of names — countable, since you can call roll number 1, 2, 3... one by one. But if you try to list every decimal number between 0 and 1 (0.001, 0.0011, 0.00111...), you will never finish — that's uncountable.",
          "worked": "Example: A = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5} — you can count each member (1st, 2nd, 3rd...), so A is <strong>countable</strong> (and finite). Now try to list every decimal number between 0 and 1: 0.1, 0.01, 0.001, 0.0001 ... you will <strong>never</strong> finish listing them one by one — that set is <strong>uncountable</strong>.",
